*   **W-2 Work Expenses:** Under current tax law (TCJA), unreimbursed employee expenses for W-2 workers are **no longer deductible**. 

Since your total itemized deductions would be far below $14,600, taking the standard deduction is the most beneficial choice. Because you are taking the standard deduction, you unfortunately cannot deduct the $1,500 charitable donation.

### 2. What You CAN Deduct (Against your 1099 Income)
While you can't itemize personal deductions, you **can** deduct business expenses against your $16,300 freelance writing income on Schedule C. This lowers your taxable business income and your self-employment tax.

*   **Home Office Deduction:** You have two ways to calculate this for your 170 sq ft exclusive-use office:
